{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "ONE pricing truth for e-Stamp partner/API orders. Core computes it (quote-components.ts, stamp-quote.service.ts, partner-estamp.service.ts); the gateway sandbox and the developer docs must reproduce it. Money is in rupees. Per e-stamp PAPER: Rs 99 procurement + Rs 5 API charge + convenience fee (default 5% of that paper's FULL duty, only when the duty is strictly above Rs 1,000); quantity multiplies the duty and every per-paper charge. GST 18% is on the fees only and is collected at Service wallet top-up. An order debits the Service wallet with the fees BEFORE GST and the Stamp duty wallet with duty x quantity. Never edit a copy: change Core's file, then copy it byte-for-byte (see README note, scripts/check-golden-pricing-sync.mjs).",
  "currency": "INR",
  "priceBook": {
    "procurementFee": 99,
    "apiPaperFee": 5,
    "convenienceFee": {
      "type": "PERCENT_ABOVE_THRESHOLD",
      "value": 5,
      "threshold": 1000
    },
    "gstPercent": 18
  },
  "fields": {
    "pricing": "Optional overrides, resolved organisation > state > default: org {convenienceFee, procurementFee, perPaperFee}, state {code, convenienceFee, procurementFee, quantityTiers}, defaults {convenienceFee}. Absent = the price book above. A convenience fee of value 0 is an explicit switch-off.",
    "lines": "Input: duty is the government duty of ONE paper; quantity (default 1) is identical papers on the line.",
    "expected": "lines[i]: unit = per-paper amounts; procurement/apiCharge/convenience = line totals; fees = line fees before GST; gst = GST on the line fees (once per line); duty = duty x quantity; total = duty + fees + gst. order = sums. wallets = what the two wallets are debited. quote = the totals POST /v1/estamp/orders/validate returns."
  },
